cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Docket: hard caps and tamper-evident receipts for AI agent runs"
message: "If you use Docket or its receipt format in academic work or in a product, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Docket contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/docket-dev-org/docket"
url: "https://github.com/docket-dev-org/docket"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/docket-dev-org/docket/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  Docket supervises an AI agent process, enforces hard caps on spending, tokens, model calls
  and wall-clock time at the provider boundary, and records model calls, tool calls,
  filesystem changes, egress decisions and process lifecycle events into an append-only,
  hash-chained ledger. Each run produces a receipt whose integrity, event order and cost
  totals can be verified offline by a third party using the format specification and
  conformance vectors in this repository, including by an independent implementation in a
  different programming language.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - provenance
  - tamper-evident
  - audit
  - llm-cost
  - transparency-log
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
